      "concept": "Complex exponentials are eigenfunctions of linear time-invariant systems, meaning they pass through filters with their frequency unchanged, altered only in amplitude and phase.",
      "figureType": "diagram",
      "learningObjectives": [
        "The student will understand that the output frequency of an LTI system is always identical to its input frequency when driven by a complex exponential.",
        "The student will be able to explain how the system's transfer function H[u] scales the amplitude via its magnitude response and shifts the wave via its phase response.",
        "The student will be able to predict how low-pass and high-pass filters selectively attenuate or phase-shift signals of different spatial frequencies."
      ],
      "keyInsight": "An LTI system cannot create new frequencies; it acts as a frequency-by-frequency volume and shift control, scaling and delaying the input without altering its fundamental shape.",
      "interactions": [
        {
          "id": "inputFrequency",
