          "effect": "Toggles the system H[u] between a 'Low-Pass' (smooths high frequencies) and a 'High-Pass' (blocks low frequencies) profile.",
          "teaches": "Shows how the filter's frequency-domain shape directly dictates which input frequencies are preserved, amplified, or attenuated at the output."
        }
      ],
      "reconstructionNotes": "Layout as a three-part horizontal pipeline: Left (Input Waveform), Center (System Block H[u]), and Right (Output Waveform). The Input panel shows a live-generated 1D real/imaginary wave (sine/cosine). The Center block shows the mathematical symbol H[u] alongside a small, interactive plot of the system's frequency response curve (magnitude and phase) with a vertical locator line indicating the selected u₀. The Right panel plots the output wave (orange) overlaid with a dimmed, ghosted reference of the input wave (blue) to clearly show the scaling (amplitude difference) and phase shift (horizontal translation) caused by the filter."
    }
